                .obsolete = false,
                .definition = .{
                    .value = "Packed column gas chromatography uses stainless steel or glass tubes (typically 2\xe2\x80\x934 mm ID, 1\xe2\x80\x936 m length) filled with particulate packing material coated with stationary phase, enabling the separation of larger sample volumes but typically providing lower efficiency and broader peaks than capillary GC.",
