                    .{
                        .tag = "id",
                        .value = "MS:4000186",
                    },
                    .{
                        .tag = "name",
                        .value = "MS1 TIC-change quantile ratios",
                    },
                    .{
                        .tag = "def",
                        .value = "\"The log ratios of successive TIC-change quantiles. The TIC changes are the list of MS1 total ion current (TIC) value changes from one to the next scan, produced when each MS1 TIC is subtracted from the preceding MS1 TIC. A value triplet represents the original QuaMeter metrics, the log ratio of the TIC-change Q2 to Q1, Q3 to Q2, TIC-change-max to Q3. The number of values in the tuple implies the quantile mode.\" [PSI:MS]",
                    },
                    .{
                        .tag = "comment",
                        .value = "The metric informs about the dynamic range of the acquisition along the chromatographic separation. This metric evaluates the stability (similarity) of MS1 TIC values from scan to scan along the LC run. High log ratios representing very large intensity differences between pairs of scans might be due to electrospray instability or presence of a chemical contaminant.",
                    },
                    .{
                        .tag = "synonym",
                        .value = "\"MS1-TIC-Change-Q2\" RELATED [PMID:24494671]",
                    },
                    .{
                        .tag = "synonym",
                        .value = "\"MS1-TIC-Change-Q3\" RELATED [PMID:24494671]",
                    },
                    .{
                        .tag = "synonym",
